What each fault is (the sed program is in bite.sh): the coprimality test of a unit coset dropped; the constrained
printer takes level 2 whatever the condition; the fallback to kernel B removed; the idele condition "excludes 0"
reduced to "is positive"; the unit printed as stored and not in normal form; the limit on decimal exponents not
applied to the real part; the digits of the printer off by one (nk = n + k - 3).

Two earlier faults survived, and were replaced (first run of bite.sh, same day, about 03:33):
  unreduced_residue  (the reduction of the residue into 1..N in tx_unit_build removed): 0 failed checks. Not a gap:
                     adf_ucoset_set_fmpz2 reduces the residue itself (ucoset.h), so the line is redundant. It stays as
                     a second guard of the contract of the hidden function.
  content_zero       (content 0 no longer refused by tx_read...): 0 failed checks. Not a gap: adf_idele_set_parts
                     refuses r <= 0 with ADF_DOMAIN, the same status. It stays because stage 6 of conventions 8.5 is
                     decided before stage 7 and the value must not be built.
A third fault of the first run (the exact interval may touch 0: `>=` for `>`) made the process abort in
adf_idele_kernel_defect (a defect of the library reported by the library itself), and a fourth did not build (an unused
variable under -Werror); both were replaced by the faults above.
